| ClipTest for !MLT: run by Test when MLTtest$Clip names a video. The
| first second with -verbose (which decoder MLT used, and why), then the
| first 10 seconds decoded with MLT's choice of decoder and on the ARM.
Echo 6. Your clip: <MLTtest$Clip>
melt -verbose <MLTtest$Clip> out=24 -consumer null
Echo    the first 10 seconds (250 frames at 25 fps), MLT's choice of decoder
Echo start <Sys$Time>
melt <MLTtest$Clip> out=249 -consumer null
Echo end   <Sys$Time>
Echo    the same, decoded on the ARM
Set MLT_AVFORMAT_PREFER none
Echo start <Sys$Time>
melt <MLTtest$Clip> out=249 -consumer null
Echo end   <Sys$Time>
Unset MLT_AVFORMAT_PREFER
